 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
 `src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+
+## Keys and roles
+
+Requests carry `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are in the data as
+`apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`.
+
+- `viewer`: `GET` only.
+- `cook`: also `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything.
+
+No key or an unknown key is 401 (`unauthorized`); a known key without
+permission is 403 (`forbidden`).
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request other than `GET` (rejected ones too, with their status) adds an
+entry `{ at, key, method, path, status }` to `audit` in the data; `key` is the
+key's name, or null when none was recognised. `GET /audit` lists the entries
+newest first and is for managers only.
